  "text": "The DRF provides up to $200 million annually, replacing the Emergency Response Fund (ERF) and shifting focus from recovery to prevention. It emphasizes strong co-funding and implementation discipline, aligning with national, state, and local strategies. The program funds both mitigation infrastructure and systemic risk reduction projects, with a competitive, merit-based selection process.",
